# Don't send these to Docker build context
.git/
.github/
.claude/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.db
*.sqlite
.env
.env.*
!.env.template
*.md
!README.md
static-dashboard.html
deploy.sh
systemd/
.DS_Store
.gitignore
CLAUDE.md
ROADMAP.md

# Keep web/ source in the build context (the `web` Docker stage runs
# `npm ci && npm run build`), but exclude local dependency/build dirs and
# QA screenshots — the image regenerates node_modules + out from scratch.
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
web/*-screenshot.png

# ── WO-H132: parity with .gitignore ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The Docker build context is governed by THIS file and nothing else. `docker
# build` has never read .gitignore, so every pattern that lives only there is a
# path an ignored local file can take into the image — and `COPY src/ src/`,
# `COPY config/ config/` and stage 0's `COPY web/ ./` all copy directories.
#
# Measured: web/src/app/shotharness is git-ignored, was NOT listed here, and the
# Next stage compiled its pages into out/_next/static/chunks/app/shotharness/
# — carrying a live client's hostname into the image.
#
# tests/test_publish_tracked_files_only_h132.py asserts this parity, so a new
# .gitignore entry fails the suite until it is mirrored here. Keep the two in
# step; this file is the one Docker actually obeys.
# Note the `**/` prefixes. A bare `foo/` in .dockerignore matches ONLY the
# context root, where the same line in .gitignore matches at every depth — so
# the existing `__pycache__/`, `*.db` and `.DS_Store` lines above never
# excluded src/agents/__pycache__ or config/x.db at all. The `**/` forms below
# give the two files the same reach.
**/__pycache__/
# NOT `**/*.pyc`: the Cython client tarball ships .pyc WITHOUT the .py, and it
# ships this file, so a client running `docker compose build` from that tarball
# would build an image with an empty src/. __pycache__/ covers the local-junk
# case; a loose .pyc next to its .py only exists in a packaged tree.
**/*.pyo
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.pem
**/.DS_Store
**/venv/
**/node_modules/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_run.log
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov/
**/coverage.xml
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.spec.bak
**/dist/
**/build/
**/site/
**/keys/
**/license.key
# .env at ANY depth, not just the context root. config/.env is the realistic
# one: a client's credentials pasted in during a support call. The template is
# re-included after, because the image ships it.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.template
# The SPA export. Git-ignored (built at release time) and the image must use
# stage 0's FRESH export, which arrives as `COPY --from=web`. Sending a stale
# local export in the context meant `COPY src/ src/` laid it down first and the
# fresh one merged on top, leaving orphaned chunks from an older build.
src/api/static/app/
tools/license-manager/ledger.json
tools/license-manager/licenses/
tools/license-manager/*.key
sales/*.pptx
sales/*.pdf
# web/ (the Next stage's context). shotharness is the one that actually leaked.
web/src/app/shotharness/
**/.pnp
**/.pnp.js
**/next-env.d.ts
**/*-screenshot.png
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
**/playwright/.cache/
**/.env*.local
web/scripts/shot*.mjs
